---
// Shown when the news feed could not be read at all.
//
// ⚠️ DELIBERATELY NOT AN EMPTY LIST. "There are no stories" and "the database
// did not answer" are different facts, and rendering the second as the first
// is how an outage becomes invisible — the page looks fine, the reader
// concludes the feed is dead, and nothing anywhere reports a problem. The
// routes pair this with a 503 for the same reason.
---

<section class="hero" aria-label="Introduction">
  <div class="hi">
    <p class="eyebrow">Amplified Thinker</p>
    <h1 class="hero-hl">News</h1>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="news-main">
  <div class="news-error">
    <h2>The news feed isn&rsquo;t loading</h2>
    <p>Something went wrong fetching the stories. Try refreshing in a moment — everything else on the site is unaffected.</p>
  </div>
</div>
